#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::print_stderr)]
//! What the conversion memo costs and what it may not change. Two fixture projects, each replayed from its recording
//! (`memo.recording.json`, `cycles.recording.json`, made by the `record_fixture` example) and, when `TSRS_BIN` names a
//! real `tsrs`, asked live, forward and last to first:
//!
//! - `memo`: one big type under many different enclosing types. The number of round trips to the checker is held to a
//!   bound, so a memo keyed by the whole enclosing context (which converts the type again under each) fails, and a
//!   type converted again at another depth does not ask for its members or type arguments again;
#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::print_stderr)]
//! Where the checker says each prop is declared (ADR 0026 S7a): `parent`, `declarations`, tags and `composes` come from
//! its answer, not from the structural prop of the same name. The `declared` fixture, replayed from
//! `declared.recording.json` (made by the `record_fixture` example against the pinned `tsrs`) and, when `TSRS_BIN`
//! names a real `tsrs`, asked live:
//!
//! - `Button`: `tone` declared in `ButtonProps` in `Button.tsx`, `size` in `BaseProps` in `Base.ts`, each with its
//!   tags; it is made of React's `HTMLAttributes` (under an `Omit`) and `RefAttributes`;
#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::print_stderr)]
//! The checker path over a fixture project of hand-written cases (`tests/fixtures/cases`): the 14 of the checker-first
//! deep dive in `Cases.tsx`, and one component per further mapping rule in `Rules.tsx`. The answer is held to a JSON
//! snapshot made from a real `tsrs` (`tests/snapshots/`), three ways:
//!
//! - replayed from its recording (`cases.recording.json`), always: the converter's output over exactly the answers the
//!   real checker gave, with no binary;
//! - against a real `tsrs` when `TSRS_BIN` names one, which also holds the answer to be the same when the checker is
//!   asked last to first (type handles change with the order of queries; the answer may not);
//! - merged over the structural result, which puts a union's members back in the order they were written in.
//!
//! Refresh the recording and the snapshot with `cargo run -p caliper-docgen-semantic --example record_fixture --
//! $TSRS_BIN cases`, then `cargo insta review`.

#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::print_stderr)]
//! Wide types on the checker path (`tests/fixtures/families`): what the project declares is listed whole however wide,
//! and what a dependency declares is named. The fixture has an interface of 150 own fields, a package interface of 150
//! fields, and a `@types/react` stand-in whose DOM attribute interface has over a hundred properties. The answer is
//! replayed from its recording (`families.recording.json`, made by the `record_fixture` example), always, and when
//! `TSRS_BIN` names a real `tsrs` it is asked live, first to last and last to first, and must give the same bytes.

use std::time::Duration;
#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::print_stderr)]
//! The checker asks for a component by the exports the extractor recorded for it (ADR 0027), and never by its display
//! name or the module's `default`. The `exports` fixture, replayed from `exports.recording.json` (made by the
//! `record_fixture` example against `typescript@7.1.0-beta`) and, when `TSRS_BIN` names a real `tsrs`, asked live:
//!
